    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated in a cul-de-sac overlooking a large green area in the established residential development of Dalcassian Park, just off the Turnpike, this three-bedroom mid-terrace home extends to approximately 77.6 sq. m. and offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a property within walking distance of Ennis town centre.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, main reception room with open fireplace, fitted kitchen/dining room and ground floor bathroom. At first floor level are three bedrooms, all benefiting from built-in wardrobes, together with additional landing storage. The property is serviced by oil-fired central heating, mains water and mains sewage.\n\nExternally, the property enjoys an enclosed front garden with mature hedging and pedestrian access, while the fully enclosed rear garden features a gravelled area and two sheds. The larger shed benefits from access to the rear laneway and is suitable for vehicle storage.\n\nThe property's central location offers convenient access to the many amenities of Ennis, including shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, primary and secondary schools, and sporting and recreational facilities. Ennis bus and rail stations are also within easy reach, while the nearby Ennis Bypass and M18 motorway provide excellent connectivity to Shannon, Limerick and Galway.\n\nWith its cul-de-sac setting and convenient town centre location, this property would make an ideal home for first-time buyers, young families or those wishing to downsize, while also offering excellent investment potential.\n\nViewing strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 5.45m x 1.8m\nTimber style flooring, carpeted timber railed stairs leading to first floor landing incorporating under stair storage, dado rail, door to coat closet and doors to main reception, kitchen dining and main bathroom.\n\nLiving Room - 3.80m x 2.6m\nSolid timber flooring, front aspect window, dado rail and open fire place with brick insert and timber surround.\n\nKitchen Breakfast Room - 3.8m x 3.6m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, rear door access, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, eye level glass display unit, one and a half bowl sink unit, integrated oven, hob and extractor hood and fan and space and plumbing for fridge freezer and dishwasher and decorative radiator cover.\n\nMain Bathroom - 1.8m x 1.7m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, part wall timber panelling, low level wc, wash hand basin, corner fitted bath with tile surround and overhead electric shower and integrated storage.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 4.45m x 1.8m\nCarpeted flooring, front aspect window, doors to all three bedrooms and door to storage closet.\n\nBedroom One - 2.7m x 2.4m\nCarpeted flooring, rear aspect window and built-in wardrobe with base drawers.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.6m 3.4m\nCarpeted flooring, rear aspect window, built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails, base drawers and overhead storage and additional built-in desk area with overhead storage.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.8m 2.7m\nCarpeted flooring, front aspect window, built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and additional base drawers.\n\nOutside - \nFront - Walled boundaries to the front and side with gated pedestrian access leading to the front door with a lawn area and mature hedging.Rear - Block wall boundaries, rear lane access, gravel area and two sheds.Shed one - 6m x 3m - rear lane access and suitable for vehicle storage.Shed two - Houses the oil boiler and sink.\n\n"
      },
      {
